{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419787-shen-motif-and-alchemy-what","id":1419787,"title":"Shen Motif and Alchemy: what?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-23T08:02:58-07:00","id":1419787,"title":"Shen Motif and Alchemy: what?","content":"I'm Canadian-Chinese, so my grasp of Chinese mythology isn't the greatest, but I grew with a lot of Chinese cinema and do read translated webnovels. As part of the process in which they enact marvels, why is alchemy the thing? I don't think many people would know the difference between Western and Chinese alchemy for one, and as someone who is aware of the difference, I'm still puzzled by what they mean exactly. What does concocting pills and elixirs according to the five elements have to do with manifesting divine miracles? What about manipulating the internal energies inside of your own body have to do with manifesting divine miracles? Why is it only the five elements and not also yin and yang?<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I'm not saying that whoever wrote that blurb about the Shen motif is wrong, I just don't understand their thought process. Anyone well-versed in Chinese mythology able to shine some light on this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T10:14:35-07:00","id":1419807,"title":"","content":"Are you suggesting to use a Chi manipulation motif?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T10:34:18-07:00","id":1419809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419787-shen-motif-and-alchemy-what?p=1419807#post1419807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you suggesting to use a Chi manipulation motif?</div> </div> </div> </div>Qi manipulation is already part of Internal Alchemy, which Talam disagrees with as a Motif.<br /> <br /> Honestly, while there can obviously be many Motif ideas for any Pantheon, I'm honestly not entirely sure what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"723\" data-vbnamecard=\"723\">Talam</a>'s problem with the Motif is, even after reading their original post. Why should alchemy <i>not</i> be fitting for the Motif? Why <i>can't</i> you produce miracles by whipping out the samadhi fire you've produced within your body, by releasing all the qi you have stored through careful body manipulation, by lighting the fuse on the alchemical concoction you have prepared? I'm not saying it's <i>the</i> perfect, all-encompassing Motif for the Sh\u00e9n - ultimately, nothing can be, because Chinese culture is uniquely multi-facetted in the way it has adapted to and adopted from many others, and thus there is even less of a one-size-fits-all for them than for anyone else. But alchemy seems no worse a fit to me than other options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T14:29:51-07:00","id":1419844,"title":"","content":"I think what I disagree with is that Chinese alchemy, which is distinct from Western alchemy and probably what most people are familiar with, is a very specific kind of thing and it's being used in a very broad manner. Now, gut instinct is to say &quot;That's not how that works&quot; BUT I might be wrong. Maybe I am ignorant of the writer meant when they used the term alchemy. Maybe my understanding of alchemy is a much narrower version of what Chinese alchemy encompasses. I don't understand, so I want to know what the thought process was for using alchemy as the motif, because maybe if someone shed light on it, I'd be &quot;Like, oh that makes sense then.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because to me, I can see Chinese alchemy cover some things, but what about Feng Shui and Fulu? Why not mention those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T16:28:23-07:00","id":1419861,"title":"","content":"It kinda does, doesn't it? Like it mentions the manipulation of the energies both within and without of the body.<br /> <br /> It also specifically mentions that it does this through exercises or concoctions.<br /> <br /> So like... In its very phrasing it's suggesting that it's using a broader definition of 'Alchemy' than a western association might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T17:53:33-07:00","id":1419877,"title":"","content":"China was always more focused on internal alchemy. When Christians discovered <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabbalah\" target=\"_blank\">Kabbalah</a> it made western internal alchemy a spiritual/religious thing unconnected to the bodies it transformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T20:06:44-07:00","id":1419899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419787-shen-motif-and-alchemy-what?p=1419861#post1419861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kinda does, doesn't it? Like it mentions the manipulation of the energies both within and without of the body.<br /> <br /> It also specifically mentions that it does this through exercises or concoctions.<br /> <br /> So like... In its very phrasing it's suggesting that it's using a broader definition of 'Alchemy' than a western association might have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having looked into Chinese alchemy, especially Neidan which is the internal alchemy, exercises seems to mean like actual exercises and not just practices in general. And concoctions is concoctions, like medicine and elixirs. So I'm having a hard time visualizing how certain exercises or medicines allow you to create a miracle of the Chaos purview for example.<br /> <br /> Like, if they just said &quot;Manipulate the energies both within and without the body according to the five elements&quot;, I'd have a pretty clear idea of what they're going for and how things would look. But &quot;alchemy&quot;, &quot;exercises&quot; and &quot;concoctions&quot; suggest a particular thing and I can't figure out what they're getting at. Like, how would I express the Mandate of Heaven through this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":723,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","user":"Talam","date":". 10-23-2020, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T20:31:30-07:00","id":1419903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419787-shen-motif-and-alchemy-what?p=1419899#post1419899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, how would I express the Mandate of Heaven through this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Brewing a potion that you give to an enemy commander a blessing, allowing their coup to succeed, thus enabling a regime change? (War, using the Concoction part of the Motif)<br /> <br /> <i>or</i><br /> <br /> Doing an exercise like some form of tai chi to manipulate the <i>qi</i> of your surroundings thus causing a collapse in a local government? (Chaos, using the Exercises part of the Motif)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T22:18:34-07:00","id":1419916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419787-shen-motif-and-alchemy-what?p=1419903#post1419903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brewing a potion that you give to an enemy commander a blessing, allowing their coup to succeed, thus enabling a regime change? (War, using the Concoction part of the Motif)<br /> <br /> <i>or</i><br /> <br /> Doing an exercise like some form of tai chi to manipulate the <i>qi</i> of your surroundings thus causing a collapse in a local government? (Chaos, using the Exercises part of the Motif)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I guess? I'll admit, you can make it work. But man, it feels like an awkward fit when &quot;altering Feng Shui&quot; as the method can work for both examples and fits better. And I think where my &quot;Wait, what?&quot; comes from is that the book is trying to use alchemy as a one-size fits all solution. You can make it work, but some use cases are kind of weak to me, so it makes me wonder why someone decided on only alchemy instead of incorporating more elements or abstracting it a little more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T23:58:53-07:00","id":1419925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1419787-shen-motif-and-alchemy-what?p=1419844#post1419844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what about Feng Shui and Fulu? Why not mention those?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always homebrew things as working in those ways in your games, I don't anyone would really disagree with that. Only issue with the former is that one of the new Pantheons in the Demigod book uses essentially the same thing as Feng Shui for their Motif.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}